    "Eight serial fresh source-to-Object primary observations in ABBA then BAAB order, identical 60 runtime flags and compiler build profile. No cached Object or decoded-only substitute.",
    "Builds, tests, screens, fixtures, hashing, copying and packet work do not overlap primary timing. All source, MBC, Object and complete metadata bytes match the qualified program in both screens and every primary observation; fourteen successful fixture pairs also match all four files.",
    "Only private frontend draft ownership, borrowing and pure immutable schema/error canonicalization change. Mutation invalidates the exact-owner cache including unique owners. Public Core SchemaDraft, grammar, language, checked errors, finite admission, current shape/factory/visit/ownership proofs and direct scalar emission remain unchanged.",
    "Final source passes 64 frontend tests including four production-module owner tests, plus two codec tests. An earlier standalone run of those four owner tests is duplicate coverage and precedes four test-fixture constructor repairs. Integration failures and their raw diagnostics remain.",
    "Both balanced blocks improve compiler time. Every candidate compiler/process/instruction/RSS observation is below every control. Native and parse mean times and several native substage means are adverse and retained. Finite cohorts are descriptive, not population estimates.",
